BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: Sunset Boulevard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T150000
UID:697100d291e4576f847dd9ae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An aging silent film queen refuses to accept that her stardom 
 has ended. She hires a young screenwriter to help set up her movie comebac
 k. The screenwriter believes he can manipulate her\, but he soon finds out
  he is wrong. The screenwriters ambivalence about their relationship and h
 er unwillingness to let go leads to a situation of violence\, madness\, an
 d death.\nAges 12+ (No official rating)\n1 Hour 50 Minutes
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, FCCR (First-Floor Auditorium)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697100d291e4576f847dd9ae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIY Nights: Craft and Socials
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260626T190000
UID:6963eb2ac967cb4120814845@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for a fun\, low stress way to try new crafts and meet 
 fellow makers? Join us for DIY Night: Craft & Socials\, a monthly adult cr
 afting program featuring a new project each month. Learn something new\, w
 ork at your own pace\, and enjoy casual conversation in a welcoming space.
  Materials are provided\, and beginners are always welcome.\nRegistration 
 is required due to limited supply. However drop in on the day of is welcom
 ed for vacant spots.\nTime: Fourth Friday of each month from 5-7\nUpcoming
  Events:\nMay 22: Perler Beads\nCraft your heart's content with Perler bea
 ds\, creating colorful designs by fusing small beads with heat.\nApril 24
 : Cross stitching\nUnleash your creativity with cross-stitching\, weaving 
 intricate designs into fabric with every stitch.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Sanderson\, Program Room on Main Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6963eb2ac967cb4120814845
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
