BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memoirs of Pause by Nanhee Kim
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T235959
UID:69e8e6edb6c4ac1fedce0186@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:"Nanhee Kim is a multi-disciplinary artist\, fashion/textile d
 esigner and educator based in Toronto. Her professional experience includ
 es working as an assistant professor at Toronto Metropolitan University’
 s School of Fashion and as a fashion designer in New York City and Vancouv
 er.\n"My work is inspired by the ephemeral tranquility\, escapism and inne
 r peace that nature provides to people. I reimagine visual narratives to 
 depict the feelings and emotions that people experience when interacting w
 ith nature\," observes Kim.\nThis exhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\np
 rogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to exhibit
  their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to reflect th
 e diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhi
 bit can be viewed during Deer Park Branch open hours. Please check the Br
 anch page before your visit.\nFree. All are welcome.\nAccessibility\nLive 
 or automated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, intervenor
  services\, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submi
 t your request at least 2 weeks in advance to:\ntpl.ca/accessibility-event
 s\n.
LOCATION:Deer Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e8e6edb6c4ac1fedce0186
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
