BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Keiko Honda Author Talk: Asian Heritage Month
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T190000
UID:696d3860992fc18a86de1e43@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Keiko Honda -a scientist\, writer\, community organizer a
 nd painter and author of\nAccidental Blooms\nas she discusses her latest 
 two books\,\nThe broken map home : escaping Korea : 1945\nand\nHidden Flow
 ers: A Memoir\n.\nKeiko's captivating story of resilience\, self-discovery
 \, and the power of community in the face of adversity seeks to inspire pe
 ople to view their challenges as an opportunity for growth. The memoir is 
 a powerful testament to the importance of community and self-discovery in 
 navigating life's challenges.\nHidden Flowers: A Memoir\nwill be for sale 
 for $29.95 and\nThe broken map home : escaping Korea : 1945\nwill be for s
 ale for $22. Cash and card payment accepted.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
