SUMMARY:Sweetgrass Medicine Mist: An Infusion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T150000
UID:69de8a49b6c4ac1fedcc546e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, participants will learn about the significa
 nce of sweetgrass from Indigenous perspective. Participants will also make
  a sweetgrass infusion that will later be strained and bottled to become a
  mist. All supplies are provided.\nDrop-in\, no registration required. Pro
 gram will be capped at the first 15 participants. Tickets will be handed o
 ut 30 minutes prior to start time.\nTanya Gluvakov is a mixed Mohawk woman
  from Toronto with family and "roots" from Six Nations of the Grand River 
 in Oshweken\, Ontario. The founder of Roots and Raven\, Tanya is a herbali
 st\, a mom\, a teacher\, and auntie\, who teaches several workshops about 
 medicines from the land and how connecting with them helps us find our way
 . She also leads several projects that bring the resurgence of medicines a
 nd accessibility to urban communities.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de8a49b6c4ac1fedcc546e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cyanotype Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T113000
UID:69e6c1195c04bc0fc062fcbe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What materials and processes existed before Adobe Photoshop? J
 oin us for a hands-on analog image making workshop to create a Cyanotype. 
 The Cyanotype is a photographic printing technique sensitive to a limited 
 near ultraviolet and blue light spectrum. It involves layering objects and
  transparencies. All are welcome!\nWe will supply all materials\, but feel
  free to bring an object or 2D silhouette for a contact print.\nInformatio
 n Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected b
 y the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(
 a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pr
 ogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libr
 ary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswe
 rline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Activity Room - First Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e6c1195c04bc0fc062fcbe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
