BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introductory Piano: Adult Learning Circles in 4 Sessions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260607T160000
UID:69e77fe6bd9a3c316a544e3f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wanted to learn to play the piano? Join us for 
 four small adult (18+ with no age limit) learning circles consisting of f
 our participants led by a professional pianist. You will learn the basic p
 iano including note recognition\, finger placing\, and simple songs. There
  will be opportunities for one-on-one instruction for each participant at 
 a baby grand piano.\nFor absolute beginners only. One time registration fo
 r all four sessions starts on Monday\, May 25\, 2026 at 10am online.  Pl
 ease do not register if you have previously participated at the piano circ
 les at the Toronto Public Library.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e77fe6bd9a3c316a544e3f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pete Crighton: The Vinyl Diaries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T200000
UID:69cd7d611e64afd01e6631f3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TPL presents author Pete Crighton in conversation at the Toron
 to Reference Library's Jack Rabinovitch Reading Room.\nIn his heartfelt me
 moir\nThe Vinyl Diaries: Sex\, Deep Cuts\, and My Soundtrack to Queer Joy\
 n\, Crighton chronicles what happened when\, in his 40s\, he finally decid
 ed to live his queer life to the fullest. But what makes this memoir sing 
 is how each new connection\, each lover\, is linked to an artist\, song\, 
 or album from his vast record collection. Kate Bush\, the B-52s\, Prince\,
  The Smiths\, Yoko Ono\, and Stevie Nicks provide an extraordinary soundtr
 ack to Crighton's mid-life sexual awakening.\nHow does music become the so
 undtrack to our most intimate moments? What role does it play in helping u
 s understand ourselves and connect with others? And what becomes possible 
 when we finally give ourselves permission to live fully—to embrace desir
 e\, take risks\, and claim the life we were always meant to have?\nJoin To
 ronto author Pete Crighton for a poignant\, funny\, and deeply personal co
 nversation about music\, memory\, and the journey to queer joy.\nQ&A and b
 ook signing to follow. Books available for purchase.\nAbout this event’s
  guests:\nPete Crighton\nRead More:\nThe Vinyl Diaries\n***\nPLAN YOUR VIS
 IT:\nLocation:\nJack Rabinovitch Reading Room\, Toronto Reference Library 
 (789 Yonge Street)\, 4th floor\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00pm\, Event starts 7:
 00pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell 
 these events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportun
 ity to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 6:45pm or until capacity is reache
 d. Seating first come\, first served\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to 
 accessibility. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to requ
 est accommodation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.c
 a or 416-393-7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nThis even
 t is part of our signature\nSalon Series\n\, where we host local and inter
 national authors\, artists and thinkers in conversation about their new bo
 oks and big ideas.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Registrants may be contacted to fill out a brief survey following t
 he program. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Y
 onge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Jack Rabinovitch Reading Room\, Toron
 to Reference Library (789 Yonge Street)\, 4th floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd7d611e64afd01e6631f3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
