BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fact or Fiction: Identifying and Combatting Misinformation and Di
 sinformation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T170000
UID:69e537d81e64afd01e6a4d94@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to separate fact from fiction in a world filled 
 with misinformation and disinformation? Join us for an interactive and ent
 ertaining program where we'll dive into the fascinating world of misinform
 ation\, exploring its origins\, impact\, and how to combat it effectively.
 \nThis program is perfect for curious minds of all ages who want to arm th
 emselves with the skills needed to navigate the complex landscape of onlin
 e information responsibly and safely.
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e537d81e64afd01e6a4d94
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Buying a Car? Know Your Rights!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T150000
UID:69e7dab2bd9a3c316a546ecb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ontario Motor Vehicle Industry Council (OMVIC) is the delegate
 d authority that oversees and regulators automotive sales in Ontario. As p
 art of our commitment to consumer protection and ensuring all residents of
  Ontario understand their rights when purchasing a vehicle\, OMVIC has dev
 eloped a presentation that we have delivered in collaboration with local s
 ervice providers across the province including libraries\, YMCA\, and newc
 omer service agencies.\nProgram Description:\nBuying a vehicle can be a ch
 allenging experience with long-term financial implications.\nJoin us for a
  presentation by the Ontario Motor Vehicle Industry Council (OMVIC) the re
 gulator of motor vehicle sales in Ontario. A representative from the OMVIC
  will provide you with resources and tips for buying new and used cars in 
 Ontario.\nTopics will include:\n•	OMVIC’s Compensation Fund\n•	Under
 standing Car Dealer Advertising\n•	Negative Equity & Long Term Loans\n
 •	Agreement & Disclosure\n•	Avoiding Curbsides & Fraud Prevention\n•
 	Tips for Buying or Leasing a Car\nDrop-in only.
LOCATION:Albion\, In the auditorium.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e7dab2bd9a3c316a546ecb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
