BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nurture & Connect: Communicating with Your Baby
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T113000
UID:69e66899b1165a41a6607285@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn practical ways to communicate with your baby and support
  early development in this free\, interactive session.\nCommunicating with
  your baby can feel like learning a new language. Practicing communication
  with your baby can help build bonds and help you better understand your b
 aby’s needs. This session will introduce simple\, practical approaches t
 o support communication and your baby’s development.\nWhat to Expect:\nU
 nderstanding Early Communication:\nLearn how babies begin to communicate a
 nd what to look for.\nBuilding Connection:\nExplore ways to strengthen you
 r bond through everyday interactions.\nPractical Tips:\nTry simple strateg
 ies to support communication and early childhood development.\nSupporting 
 Your Baby’s Growth:\nLearn how to create a responsive and supportive env
 ironment.\nThis session will be led by a Speech Language Pathologist from 
 the George Hull Centre for Children and Families\, who will share practica
 l strategies to support early communication and development.\nToronto Publ
 ic Library presents this program in collaboration with the West Toronto On
 tario Health Team (OHT)\, a network of over 40 local health and social ser
 vice providers working together to improve the health and well-being of co
 mmunities in West Toronto.\nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis free\, in-perso
 n event is part of Toronto Public Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitia
 tive.\nRegistration is preferred\, but drop-ins are welcome.\nRegister on 
 Eventbrite to reserve your spot.\nWe can't wait to see you there!
LOCATION:Mimico Centennial
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e66899b1165a41a6607285
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
