BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Movie Screening: I Like Movies
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T200000
UID:69e17936fca21471b7ef70d9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This month's feature:\nI Like Movies\nEnjoy a night at the mov
 ies! Join us for a free movie on the big screen in our accessible theatre.
 \nDescription: Socially awkward 17-year-old cinephile\, Lawrence Kweller\
 , is self-absorbed and movie-obsessed. Fully convinced he can earn $90\,00
 0 to achieve his dream of attending film school at NYU\, he gets a part-ti
 me job at Sequels video store. There older store manager\, Alana\, takes h
 im under her wing. Meanwhile Lawrence sabotages every high school relation
 ship he has with his narcissistic film snobbery. Faced with the impending 
 reality of university life\, Lawrence must change his ways.\nThis film is 
 rated 14A. 99 minutes. Start time is 6:00 pm. Drop in. All are welcome!
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre (lower level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e17936fca21471b7ef70d9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweetgrass Medicine Mist: An Infusion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T113000
UID:69cd69d1f29b90618efd16f1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, participants will learn about the significa
 nce of sweetgrass from Indigenous perspective. Participants will also make
  a sweetgrass infusion that will later be strained and bottled to become a
  mist. All supplies are provided.\nDrop-in\, no registration required. Pro
 gram will be capped at the first 15 participants.\nTanya Gluvakov is a mix
 ed Mohawk woman from Toronto with family and "roots" from Six Nations of t
 he Grand River in Oshweken\, Ontario. The founder of Roots and Raven\, Tan
 ya is a herbalist\, a mom\, a teacher\, and auntie\, who teaches several w
 orkshops about medicines from the land and how connecting with them helps 
 us find our way. She also leads several projects that bring the resurgence
  of medicines and accessibility to urban communities.
LOCATION:Jane/Sheppard
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cd69d1f29b90618efd16f1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
