SUMMARY:Book Club: Frying Plantain
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T160000
UID:69eb7e142866a5b4884a95bf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Kara Davis is a girl caught in the middle — of her Canadian 
 nationality and her desire to be a “true” Jamaican\, of her mother and
  grandmother’s rages and life lessons\, of having to avoid being thought
  of as too “faas” or too “quiet” or too “bold” or too “soft.
 ”\nJoin us for a chat about the book Frying Plantain by Zalika Reid-Bent
 a. This is a registered program\, you can register online and pick up a c
 opy of the book in branch.
LOCATION:St. Clair/Silverthorn
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69eb7e142866a5b4884a95bf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
