BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Butterflies On The Brink: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing Scree
 ning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T200000
UID:69e28789b1165a41a65fe3dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Mottled Duskywing butterfly\, found only in a handful of h
 abitats in Ontario\, is vanishing at an alarming rate. Witness the inspiri
 ng efforts of a dedicated recovery team as they work tirelessly to bring t
 his species back to its former range.\nJoin us for a screening of\nButterf
 lies on the Brink\n: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing\n\, a gripping doc
 umentary about a rare butterfly species' fight for survival on the edge of
  extinction.\nThe film is approximately 47 minutes long\, followed by a Q&
 A panel with Miles Finlayson\, the director of Butterflies On The Brink\, 
 and special guest\nAdrienne Brewster\n\, Executive Director of Cambridge 
 Butterfly Conservatory.\nPresented by the\nDavid Suzuki Foundation\n\, a C
 anadian environmental non-profit organization with a mission to protect na
 ture’s diversity and the wellbeing of all life\, now and for the future.
 \nFree. Registration required. Doors open at 6:15 pm. At 6:30 pm\, seating
  becomes first-come\, first-served until capacity is reached.\nThis progra
 m is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Frie
 nds of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nQuestions? Please conta
 ct North York Central Library - Business\, Science & Technology Department
 .\nInformation Collection Notice: The personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e28789b1165a41a65fe3dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
