BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Butterflies On The Brink: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing Scree
 ning
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260618T200000
UID:69e28787b1165a41a65fe3da@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Mottled Duskywing butterfly\, found only in a handful of h
 abitats in Ontario\, is vanishing at an alarming rate. Witness the inspiri
 ng efforts of a dedicated recovery team as they work tirelessly to bring t
 his species back to its former range.\nJoin us for a screening of\nButterf
 lies on the Brink\n: The Story of the Mottled Duskywing\n\, a gripping doc
 umentary about a rare butterfly species' fight for survival on the edge of
  extinction.\nThe film is approximately 47 minutes\, followed by a Q&A pan
 el with\nMiles Finlayson\n\, the director of Butterflies On The Brink\, wi
 th special guests:\nAdrienne Brewster\n\, Executive Director of Cambridge
  Butterfly Conservatory.\nJessica Linton\,\nSenior Biologist and Species a
 t Risk Manager at Natural Resource Solutions Inc. and the Chair of the On
 tario Butterfly Species at Risk Recovery Team.\nDr. Ryan Norris\n\, profes
 sor at the University of Guelph's Department of Integrative Biology\nPre
 sented by the\nDavid Suzuki Foundation\n\, a Canadian environmental non-pr
 ofit organization with a mission to protect nature’s diversity and the w
 ellbeing of all life\, now and for the future.\nFree. Registration require
 d. Doors open at 6:15 pm. At 6:30 pm\, seating becomes first-come\, first-
 served until capacity is reached.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Frag
 ile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Librar
 y\, South Chapter.​\nQuestions? Please contact North York Central Librar
 y - Business\, Science & Technology Department.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Theatre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e28787b1165a41a65fe3da
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spring in the Garden: Getting Your Garden Ready to Grow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260516T140000
UID:69ce9dbc5c04bc0fc0612267@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Spring is the most exciting time in the garden. The possibilit
 ies are endless – new pollinator plants\, new containers to design\, fin
 ding just the right plant that’s going to give you that one perfect toma
 to. Join a\nToronto Master Gardener\nand find out how to make these possib
 ilities a reality and enjoy the best season ever!
LOCATION:Brookbanks\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ce9dbc5c04bc0fc0612267
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
