BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nuts and Bolts of Podcasting and Introduction to Audio Editing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T200000
UID:69e9088d1e64afd01e6af390@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Amanda Cupido in this two part podcasting workshop where 
 you will learn the basics of setting up your very first podcast!\nIn the 
 first session\, you’ll get a hands-on introduction to setting up your po
 dcast using our recording studio. You’ll learn how to connect microphone
 s\, set up and use an audio interface\, and record your voice using indust
 ry-standard audio software\, giving you practical experience with the esse
 ntial tools needed to start podcasting.\nIn the second session\, you’ll 
 learn the basics of audio editing using Adobe Audition so you can polish y
 our recordings and prepare your podcast for sharing with the world. You’
 ll get hands-on practice trimming audio\, adjusting levels\, and improving
  overall sound quality to create a clean\, professional final product.\nAl
 l necessary equipment will be provided.\nPlease arrive\n5-10 minutes\nbefo
 re the program. If you are more than 5 minutes late\, your spot will be f
 orfeited.
LOCATION:Albion\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e9088d1e64afd01e6af390
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spoken Word Series with Andrea Thompson Workshop 4: Review and Re
 hearsal (REGISTRATION FULL)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T200000
UID:698a3bde4a9fd98b7f7d0bab@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Workshop 1: The Craft of Poetry\nThursday April 30 - Jack Rab
 inovitch Reading Room - Participants will explore the fundamentals of crea
 ting well-crafted\, evocative poetry with the use of techniques like senso
 ry details\, extended metaphor\, figurative language\, sound devices and m
 ore.\nWorkshop 2: Finding Your Voice\nThursday May 7 - Jack Rabinovitch R
 eading Room - Participants will explore strategies to help develop their o
 wn unique poetic voice and write courageously about issues affecting their
  own individual daily lives.\nWorkshop 3: Poetry in Performance\nThursday 
 May 14 - Jack Rabinovitch Reading Room - Participants will focus on strate
 gies and techniques to create powerful poetry performances\, overcome stag
 e fright and bring their writing to life on the stage.\nWorkshop 4: Review
  and Rehearsal\nThursday May 21 - Beeton Hall - Participants will prepare 
 and rehearse for the final showcase event.\nThis program series is present
 ed by Andrea Thompson\, TPL’s Spring 2026 Writer in Residence whose focu
 s is Spoken Word Poetry for an Adult Audience. Learn more about TPL's\nWri
 ter in Residence\nprogram\, including upcoming programs and one-on-one con
 sultation sessions.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Workshops 1-3 will be in the Jack Rab
 inovitch Reading Room (fourth floor). Workshop 4 will be in Beeton Hall (f
 irst floor).
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698a3bde4a9fd98b7f7d0bab
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
