BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:South Asian Romance & Love Stories - a talk with author Sonya Sing
 h!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260505T200000
UID:69e532691e64afd01e6a4a9a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bestselling Canadian author Sonya Singh explores love\, fami
 ly and modern romance through a South Asian lens. Drawing from her newest 
 novel\nThe Fake Matchmaker\nas well as her debut novel\nSari\, Not Sari\n\
 , she examines the complexities of cultural expectations\, identity and re
 lationships across different stages of life. Through humour\, honesty and 
 heartfelt storytelling\, she unpacks familiar romantic tropes\, the pressu
 res of family and community\, and the idea of second chances in love. Sing
 h also reflects on how South Asian love stories are evolving in contempora
 ry fiction\, moving beyond stereotypes to more nuanced\, authentic portray
 als.\nThe talk includes a live reading from her work followed by an engagi
 ng audience Q&A.\nAll are welcome!
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e532691e64afd01e6a4a9a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
