BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Journalism Series with David Silverberg: What do editors want from
  freelance journalists? (panel discussion)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260616T193000
UID:69c81fe8b48451fc3c0bd8f7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This panel discussion is presented by the North York Central 
 Library's 2026 Writer in Residence David Silverberg\, whose focus is on Jo
 urnalism.\nLearn from editors who have witnessed it all. Joining David on 
 a panel discussion to share their insight on ideas they’d like to see fr
 om freelance journalists\, Toronto-based editors Navneet Alang (opinions 
 editor\, The Toronto Star) and Judith Pereira (arts editor\, The Globe & 
 Mail) will reveal their favourite pitches and discuss the types of articl
 es they publish. The panel will also discuss pay rates\, developing relati
 onships with editors and their top Do’s and Don’ts.\nThis discussion w
 ill be followed by Q&A\nLearn more about TPL's\nWriter in Residence\nprogr
 am\, including upcoming programs and one-on-one consultation sessions.\nIn
 formation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is col
 lected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sect
 ions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for even
 t and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how 
 the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff a
 t\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 
 2G8.
