BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fire Safety & Fall Prevention for Older Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T190000
UID:69cc324a1e64afd01e65f05e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An outreach program to help older adults learn how to stay saf
 e at home. This program includes fire safety and fall prevention education
  designed and delivered in partnership with Toronto Fire Services. The pro
 gram will include placement of smoke and CO alarms\, escape planning for s
 pecial needs\, fire safety in high rise buildings\, causes of home fires a
 nd\, calling for help.\nRegistration is encouraged on TPL's website. Drop-
 ins welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cc324a1e64afd01e65f05e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Interviewing Skills with ACCES Employment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260520T150000
UID:69cc32558089f23c6765d81c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join ACCES Employment to understand the purpose and structure 
 of an interview as well as the different types of interviews and interview
  questions that you may encounter.  The session will also cover what to do
  before\, during and after an interview to make the best impression.\nRegi
 stration is encouraged on TPL website.\nDrop-ins welcome until capacity is
  reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on thi
 s form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librari
 es Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be 
 used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questio
 ns about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answe
 rline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, To
 ronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cc32558089f23c6765d81c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:LSP: English Conversation Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260430T123000
UID:69cc385224bd39b0b5e60392@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join our English Conversation Circle\, a friendly space where 
 newcomers can practice speaking English and build confidence. It is open t
 o beginner and intermediate learners\, and we focus on everyday conversati
 ons\, useful vocabulary\, and simple activities. It’s a great way to mee
 t new people and feel more connected to your community.\nNote: This is not
  a formal language class. Refreshments will be served.\nIn partnership wi
 th Immigration\, Refugees and Citizenship Canada\, TNO - The Neighbourhoo
 d Organization & Toronto Public Library.
LOCATION:Thorncliffe
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cc385224bd39b0b5e60392
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
