BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nuts and Bolts of Podcasting and Introduction to Audio Editing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260514T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260514T200000
UID:69e9088d1e64afd01e6af391@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join Amanda Cupido in this two part podcasting workshop where 
 you will learn the basics of setting up your very first podcast!\nIn the 
 first session\, you’ll get a hands-on introduction to setting up your po
 dcast using our recording studio. You’ll learn how to connect microphone
 s\, set up and use an audio interface\, and record your voice using indust
 ry-standard audio software\, giving you practical experience with the esse
 ntial tools needed to start podcasting.\nIn the second session\, you’ll 
 learn the basics of audio editing using Adobe Audition so you can polish y
 our recordings and prepare your podcast for sharing with the world. You’
 ll get hands-on practice trimming audio\, adjusting levels\, and improving
  overall sound quality to create a clean\, professional final product.\nAl
 l necessary equipment will be provided.\nPlease arrive\n5-10 minutes\nbefo
 re the program. If you are more than 5 minutes late\, your spot will be f
 orfeited.
LOCATION:Albion\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e9088d1e64afd01e6af391
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Practically Applying Cancer Nutrition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T203000
UID:69e917f74dacf581ff8a74ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to apply evidence-based nutrition strategies in canc
 er care through practical guidance and a live culinary demonstration.\nNut
 rition and its practical application play a vital role in cancer care\, ye
 t they are often overlooked. Evidence-based cancer nutrition guidelines em
 phasize the importance of eating well not only to help prevent cancer\, bu
 t also to support treatment\, manage side effects\, and reduce the risk of
  recurrence. This session will explore how nutrition can be applied in rea
 l\, practical ways across different stages of cancer care.\nWhat to Expect
 :\nUnderstanding Cancer Nutrition:\nLearn how nutrition supports cancer pr
 evention\, treatment\, and recovery.\nPractical Application:\nExplore how 
 to apply evidence-based nutrition strategies in everyday life.\nCulinary D
 emonstration:\nWatch a live demonstration focused on preparing nutritious\
 , supportive meals.\nResources and Guidance:\nLearn about evidence-based t
 ools and resources to support informed nutrition choices.\nThis session wi
 ll be led by Amy Symington\, M.Sc.\, a nutrition professor\, author\, rese
 archer\, and culinary nutrition program coordinator at Gilda’s Toronto. 
 She also works with the University Health Network and the Canadian Liver F
 oundation\, bringing both academic and practical experience in cancer nutr
 ition.\nToronto Public Library presents this program in collaboration with
  the West Toronto Ontario Health Team (OHT)\, a network of over 40 local h
 ealth and social service providers working together to improve the health 
 and well-being of communities in West Toronto.\nYour Health Matters\nThis 
 program is part of Toronto Public Library’s\nYour Health Matters\ninitia
 tive\, which focuses on providing trusted programs and resources to help p
 eople make informed decisions about their health. Learn more by exploring 
 the\nYour Health Matters web page\n.\nReserve Your Spot Today!\nThis virtu
 al event is free to join but registration is required.\nPlease register on
  Eventbrite\n.\nOnce registered\, you’ll receive an email with details o
 n how to join the session.\nWe can’t wait to see you there!
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e917f74dacf581ff8a74ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Employment Workshop with YES
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T123000
UID:69e929f8b1165a41a660fcfe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for employment? Join YES (Youth Employment Services) f
 or an informative workshop on writing your resume and updating your interv
 iew skills.\nRegistration required\, all ages welcome. Visit\nhttps://www.
 yes.on.ca/program/workshops/\nto register.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room B/C
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e929f8b1165a41a660fcfe
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tuesday Night Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T194500
UID:69e92a47129f1274383a35a9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Tuesday\, May 26\, at 6:30 p.m. to enjoy a c
 up of tea and talk about our book of the month\,\nAn elderly lady is up to
  no good\n\,\nby Helene Tursten.\nMaud is an irascible 88-year-old woman w
 ith no family\, no friends\, and... no qualms about a little murder. This 
 funny\, irreverent story collection by Helene Tursten\, author of the Iren
 e Huss investigations\, features two-never-before translated stories that 
 will keep you laughing all the way to the retirement home. Over the course
  of her adventures--or misadventures--this little bold lady will handle a 
 crisis with a local celebrity who has her eyes on Maud's apartment\, foil 
 the engagement of her long-ago lover\, and dispose of some pesky neighbors
 .\nIf you prefer an eBook or eAudiobook\, ask library staff how to access 
 them. All are welcome!  Drop-in\, registration not required.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, First floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e92a47129f1274383a35a9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T130000
UID:69e92c5bbd9a3c316a54b245@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This\n program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn
  new skills\, and \nhave fun. It involves peer-led group activities which 
 can include crafts\, games\,\n walking\, yoga\, and more. Meet new folks\
 , build social connections\, and tell us\n about programs and services you
  would like to see in the neighbourhood!\nOn Fridays\, join us for crafts 
 (11am - 1pm)\, exercise (11:30am - 12:30pm)\, and Ozzy the therapy dog (al
 ternate Fridays).\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all participan
 ts. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis program is i
 n collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e92c5bbd9a3c316a54b245
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
