BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From Our Mouths to Your Ears: Generate Music from Sound with AI To
 ols
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T160000
UID:69a202864dacf581ff7e6766@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could hum a melody\, tap a rhythm on a table\, or 
 beatbox a groove - and have AI turn it into a fully produced piece of musi
 c? Some of today's AI music tools can interpret sounds you make with your 
 voice and body and transform them into original compositions.\nIn this hig
 h-energy session\, you'll sing\, clap\, beatbox\, and tap your way into cr
 eating music using nothing but your own sounds as a starting point. It's o
 ne of the fastest and most fun ways to go from an idea in your head to a f
 inished track. No musical training is required\; just a willingness to mak
 e some noise.\nThis program is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and 
 Music Production) program\, which is designed to help beginner and interme
 diate learners build knowledge and creative skills and get hands-on with c
 urrent AI tools in music production and learn about the history\, copyrigh
 t and ethics of generative music. For more information and a full list of 
 programs\, visit\ntpl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Digital Innovation Hub\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a202864dacf581ff7e6766
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vibe-Code with AI for Music Generation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T160000
UID:69a203164dacf581ff7e677a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could describe the kind of music tool you want in 
 plain English and have AI build it for you - no coding experience needed? 
 This approach\, known as "vibe-coding\," lets you design custom music-gene
 rating tools simply by having a conversation with AI.\nIn this session\, y
 ou'll use AI to help you design and build your own small music-generating 
 programs that can create melodies\, rhythms\, and patterns on the fly. You
 'll learn best practices for communicating with AI to get usable results\,
  and discover how to connect multiple tools together for more complex musi
 cal possibilities. No prior music or programming experience is required.\n
 Registration is required.\nThis program is part of the Innovator in Reside
 nce (AI and Music Production) program\, which is designed to help beginner
  and intermediate learners build knowledge and creative skills and get han
 ds-on with current AI tools in music production and learn about the histor
 y\, copyright and ethics of generative music. For more information and a f
 ull list of programs\, visit\ntpl.ca/airesident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Digital Innovation Hub\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a203164dacf581ff7e677a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Generate Music with Gesture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260617T180000
UID:69a203be1e64afd01e5e90f0@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could create music just by waving your hands\, mov
 ing your body\, or holding up an object? In this workshop\, you'll discove
 r how AI and motion-sensing technology can turn real-world movements into 
 ever-changing soundscapes.\nYou'll use AI to generate original ambient sou
 nd materials\, then connect them to a visual program that responds to your
  gestures\, movements\, and even objects in the room - turning your body i
 nto a musical instrument. No prior music or programming experience is requ
 ired.\nRegistration is required.\nThis program is part of the Innovator in
  Residence (AI and Music Production) program\, which is designed to help b
 eginner and intermediate learners build knowledge and creative skills and 
 get hands-on with current AI tools in music production and learn about the
  history\, copyright and ethics of generative music. For more information 
 and a full list of programs\, visit tpl.ca/airesident.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Digital Innovation Hub\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69a203be1e64afd01e5e90f0
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) Info Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260525T190000
UID:69ea4c8366c3387a9d07ade8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more?\nDrop in for the information session on Mo
 nday\, May 25 from 5-7 pm\n.\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Monday\,\nonce 
 a week for 8 weeks\, June 1 - July 20\, 2026\, 5-8 pm\n.\nRegistration clo
 ses after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSn
 acks and refreshments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists 
 will be available at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\
 nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initiative\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is sol
 ely responsible for the protection of \npersonal information collected thr
 ough the program registration \nprocess.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ea4c8366c3387a9d07ade8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
