DESCRIPTION:Whether you're a beginner or an experienced artist\, our Artis
 ts Circle program offers a welcoming space to reduce stress\, explore new 
 art techniques\, and connect with fellow art appreciators. Each month\, t
 he library will set out a selection of art books based on a chosen theme.
  We will provide participants with an artistic prompt and materials to cr
 eate their artwork.\nCelebrate the colour and beauty of springtime florals
  with paper flowers that were made to last! Learn how to craft paper ros
 es or peonies to take home or give to a friend. All materials provided\; 
 no experience necessary.\nNote:\nYour spot will not be guaranteed if you a
 rrive more than 10 minutes after the start of the program.\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline
 @tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69df8e19b6c4ac1fedcc846c
