BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Asian Heritage Movie: In the Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T193000
UID:69ebbc274dacf581ff8ae8fc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of\nIn the Room\,\nA National Film Boa
 rd of Canada production.\nIn the face of exile and erasure\, this artistic
 ally crafted documentary features testimonies from five Afghan women whose
  courage and conviction transcend borders. Through a series of deeply pers
 onal conversations filmed in intimate spaces\, director Brishkay Ahmed wea
 ves together stories of resistance\, exile\, and self-discovery. From cele
 brated singer Mozhdah Jamalzadah to director and activist Nelofer Pazira-F
 isk\, each woman reflects on what it means to speak—and survive—as an 
 Afghan woman in a world that continuously attempts to silence them. As the
  Taliban’s return to power threatens to erase decades of progress\,\nIn 
 the Room\nbecomes both a record of resilience and a cautionary tale for wo
 men everywhere: the fight for freedom is never over\nScreening in English
 \, Dari\, Farsi with English subtitles\nReleased in 2025\, rated 14+\, 1hr
  15 mins.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ebbc274dacf581ff8ae8fc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Animals to Abstract Artwork by Jackie Lewis
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260501T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T235959
UID:69ed072bc1cf6f9a7587c43f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of May\, the works of artist Jackie Lewis
  are on display at Leaside branch in an exhibit titled\nAnimals to Abstrac
 t Artwork\n.\nJackie was always the class artist in school and won three
  Lions Club awards for their art. They studied art with James Spencer who 
 has two of his mountain paintings in the National Gallery in Ottawa. They
  have made art work for thirty years.\n"I am very in-tune with my painting
 s channeling love and light to assist both myself and the viewer."\nThis e
 xhibit is part of\nTPL's Art Exhibit\nprogram. Toronto Public Library prov
 ides space for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the
  city. These exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the
  city and its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nLeaside B
 ranch\nopen hours. Please check the Leaside Branch page before your visit.
 \nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Artist: Jackie Lewis\; Title of Pi
 ece: Young Tiger\; Medium: Acrylic\; Size/Dimensions: up to 20 x 25 cm
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ed072bc1cf6f9a7587c43f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Behind Five Willows: Book Launch and Korean Heritage Celebration w
 ith Author June Hur
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T200000
UID:69de4114e2a2952aed0ea892@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:From the award-winning Korean-Canadian author\, June Hur\, co
 mes a warm and romantic homage to Jane Austen set in historical Korea\, ab
 out a reader and a writer who secretly fight against government book banni
 ng and find themselves irresistibly drawn together.\nJoin us for the offi
 cial global launch of\nBehind Five Willows\n\, presented in celebration 
 of Asian Heritage Month\, featuring a Korean drumming performance and pan
 sori performance\, followed by a book talk with June Hur\, in conversation
  with author Sarah Suk.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for all part
 icipants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nQuestion and
  answer session and book signing to follow. Books available for purchase.\
 nRegistration required.\nAbout this event's guests:\nJune Hur\nSarah Suk\n
 Read more:\nBehind Five Willows\nOther books by June Hur\nPlan Your Visit:
 \nLocation:\nAuditorium (2nd floor)\, North York Central Library (5120 Yo
 nge Street)\nTime:\nDoors open 6:00 pm. Event starts 6:15 pm.\nTickets:\nF
 ree registration required. Registrants access until 6:10 pm. Seating firs
 t come\, first served.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal infor
 mation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the P
 ublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information 
 will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalua
 tion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dire
 cted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yong
 e Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\nTitles related to this event\nBehind Five 
 Willows
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69de4114e2a2952aed0ea892
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
